      "correct_option": "A",
      "grounding": "The REBUS model provides a rigorous neurocomputational account of mystical experiences, therapeutic breakthroughs, and the dissolution of selfhood:\n1. **The Default Mode Network (DMN) as the Citadel of the Ego**:\n   - The DMN (including the posterior cingulate cortex, medial prefrontal cortex, and inferior parietal lobule) sits at the very apex of the cortical predictive hierarchy.\n   - It maintains our most deeply entrenched, hyper-prior models of reality:\n     - Our sense of autobiographical continuity (\"I am person $X$ with history $Y$\");\n     - The rigid separation between the subject and the objective world (\"Self vs. Other\");\n     - Mental time-travel (rumination about the past, anxiety about the future).\n2. **The Mechanism of 5-$\\text{HT}_{2\\text{A}}$ Agonism**:\n   - Classical psychedelics bind heavily to 5-$\\text{HT}_{2\\text{A}}$ receptors concentrated on **layer-V pyramidal neurons** in association cortex.\n   - This desynchronizes the normal rhythmic firing of the DMN and alpha-band oscillations.\n   - **The Entropic Brain**: Neural connectivity becomes hyper-flexible and chaotic; brain regions that normally never communicate begin cross-talking directly (underlying synesthesia).\n3. **REBUS (Relaxed Beliefs Under Psychedelics)**:\n   - High-level priors that normally constrain our perception of the world lose their **precision weighting**. The rigid cognitive scaffolding is \"melted\" or relaxed.\n   - As high-level priors weaken, bottom-up sensory prediction errors that are normally filtered out surge upward into conscious awareness.\n   - **Ego Dissolution**: When the DMN's top-down generative model of the self loses its precision weighting, the feeling of being an isolated \"I\" inside a body dissolves. The subject experiences unbounded oceanic unity, timelessness, and direct interconnectedness with nature, perfectly matching the phenomenological descriptions of Eastern non-duality (Advaita Vedānta / Buddhist *anattā*).",
      "distractor_analysis": "- **(B) is incorrect**: Classical psychedelics (psilocybin, LSD) are physically non-neurotoxic at standard doses and stimulate neuroplasticity and dendritic arborization (BDNF expression), not cellular destruction.\n- **(C) is incorrect**: Autonomic temperature fluctuations during psychedelic sessions are minor and homeostatically regulated; physical hypothermia is not the mechanism of REBUS.\n- **(D) is incorrect**: The adult cranium is a rigid bony structure; skull expansion is a physiological impossibility.",
      "reference": "Robin L. Carhart-Harris and Karl J. Friston, \"REBUS and the Anarchic Brain: Toward a Unified Model of the Brain Action of Psychedelics\", *Pharmacological Reviews* 71, no. 3 (2019): 316–344; Robin L. Carhart-Harris et al., \"Neural Correlates of the Psychedelic State as Determined by fMRI Studies with Psilocybin\", *Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences* 109, no. 6 (2012): 2138–2143."
