      "question": "In their seminal paper \"Studies in the Logic of Explanation\" (1948), Carl Hempel and Paul Oppenheim formulated the **Deductive-Nomological (DN) Model** of scientific explanation. Under this covering-law model, what structural conditions must be satisfied for an account to count as a genuine scientific explanation of a particular empirical phenomenon?",
