      "distractor_analysis": "- **(B) is incorrect**: The semantic existence of witches in jurisprudence has nothing to do with whether the universal generalization is empirically and logically true for the physical material.\n- **(C) is incorrect**: Sodium chloride ($NaCl$) readily dissolves in water due to dipole hydration; no catalyst is required.\n- **(D) is incorrect**: Dissolution is a physical phase change where ions dissociate; no mass is destroyed, and thermodynamics is not violated.",
