      "correct_option": "A",
      "grounding": "Phil Dowe's Conserved Quantity theory represents the gold standard of physicalist theories of objective causal explanation:\n1. **The Failure of Salmon's Counterfactual Mark Transmission**:\n   - Salmon claimed: A process is causal if it can transmit a mark.\n   - *Problem*: To test this, you must say: *\"If I were to mark this beam of light, the mark would persist.\"*\n   - But this relies on counterfactual conditionals! Logical empiricists and physicalists sought to ground causation in objective physical ontology, not subjective counterfactuals.\n2. **Dowe's Physicalist Axioms (CQ Theory)**:\n   - Dowe replaced counterfactuals with actual physical conservation laws:\n     - **Definition 1 (Causal Process)**: A causal process is the worldline of an object that possesses a conserved quantity.\n       - A photon moving through space possesses energy and momentum ($E = pc$). It is a causal process.\n       - A baseball flying through the air possesses mass, momentum, and charge. It is a causal process.\n       - The shadow moving along a wall (the spotlight pseudo-process) **possesses no conserved quantity**: the shadow is not an object, has no mass, carries no momentum, and exchanges zero charge along the wall!\n     - **Definition 2 (Causal Interaction)**: A causal interaction is an intersection of worldlines that involves the exchange of a conserved quantity:\n       - When a bat hits a baseball, linear momentum is transferred from bat to ball ($\\Delta p$). That exchange constitutes the causal interaction.\n3. **Salmon's Concession and Synthesis (1994)**:\n   - Wesley Salmon acknowledged the superiority of Dowe's formulation, abandoning mark transmission in favor of conserved quantities (*\"Causality without Counterfactuals\"*, 1994).\n   - This anchored scientific explanation directly in Noether’s theorem and fundamental conservation laws in physics.",
      "distractor_analysis": "- **(B) is incorrect**: The CQ theory is strictly naturalistic and physicalist; immaterial spirits possessing zero physical energy cannot be causal processes.\n- **(C) is incorrect**: Causal processes are governed by Special Relativity ($v \\le c$); super-luminal speeds are prohibited for mass-energy exchange.\n- **(D) is incorrect**: \"Conserved quantity\" in physics refers to quantities governed by conservation laws (energy, momentum, electric charge), not financial assets.",
