      "question": "In their influential paper \"Counterfactual Explanations Without Opening the Black Box: Automated Decisions and the GDPR\" (*Harvard Journal of Law & Technology*, 2017), Sandra Wachter, Brent Mittelstadt, and Chris Russell proposed **Counterfactual Explanations** to fulfill the legal and ethical requirements of the European Union General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR, Articles 13–15 and 22: \"Right to an Explanation\"). What is the precise mathematical formulation of a counterfactual explanation, and why does it uniquely provide **\"Algorithmic Recourse\"** for affected individuals?",
