      "question": "In *Human Compatible: Artificial Intelligence and the Problem of Control* (2019) and the seminal paper \"Cooperative Inverse Reinforcement Learning\" (Hadfield-Menell et al., 2016), Stuart Russell argues that the standard model of AI—where a machine is programmed to optimize a fixed, known objective—is fundamentally flawed and dangerous. How do **Assistance Games / CIRL** mathematically solve the problem of value alignment and ensure an AI remains corrigible and switch-offable?",
